# Changelog Workflow

- Any meaningful component change must update `CHANGELOG.md` in the current unreleased section (or planned release section).
- Follow Keep a Changelog format and `src/documentation/development/ReleaseWorkflow.mdx`.
- Version header format: `## [x.y.z] — YYYY-MM-DD` (or `IN FUTURE` for planned release).
- Allowed sections for new entries only:
  - `Added`
  - `Changed`
  - `Fixed`
  - `Removed`
  - `Security`
- Do not use `Updated` for new changelog records.
- For component notes, include only package-relevant changes:
  - public API changes;
  - behavior changes;
  - visual changes affecting delivered component.
- Do not include Storybook-only changes in component release notes unless package behavior is affected.
- For breaking changes, add migration guidance (what was removed/renamed and replacement).
- Evaluate release impact with each change set:
  - `patch` for fixes without public API expansion;
  - `minor` for backward-compatible features;
  - `major` for breaking changes.
